<section class="cw-container cw-grounded" aria-labelledby="cw-local-title">
  <div><p class="cw-eyebrow">On your device. At your pace.</p><h2 id="cw-local-title">Your projects<br />have a home.</h2></div>
  <div><p>Projects, source history and learning progress are stored locally. The app has no developer-hosted account, advertising or analytics. Git credentials stay in the device’s Keychain; remote Git transfers happen when you request them.</p><p>Local editing, bundled runtimes and accessible learning material work offline. On supported devices, optional on-device tools can complete an identifier, answer a question about your code or draft a Git commit summary. You review a proposed code edit before applying it.</p><details><summary>What to expect from an iPad workspace</summary><p>The project shell supports a defined set of commands. It is not an unrestricted Linux terminal, and the app does not install arbitrary native packages or extensions. Source debugging is currently for Python; C and C++ can compile and run. Keep independent copies of work you cannot afford to lose.</p></details></div>
